  "title": "CHAPTER 1: HISTORY OF UTTARAKHAND",
  "order": 1,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "nl9ztqe",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1.1 Ancient Period"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Ancient period witnessed early political rule under the Kuninda and Katyuri dynasties.",
        "Medieval history was dominated by the Parmar dynasty in Garhwal and the Chand dynasty in Kumaon.",
        "Gurkha rule extended over Kumaon in 1790 and Garhwal in 1804 before ending with the Treaty of Sugauli in 1815.",
        "The region played an active role in the Indian Freedom Movement through protests against coolie-begar and British forestry laws.",
        "Uttarakhand was officially carved out of Uttar Pradesh on November 9, 2000, becoming the 27th state of India."
      ],
      "id": "bdw97ys"
    },
